{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/57398-equipment-for-hunting-faeries","id":57398,"title":"Equipment for hunting Faeries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-25T06:46:52-08:00","id":57398,"title":"Equipment for hunting Faeries","content":"So in a couple of months we'll be seeing Mortal Remains, hunter for the GMC.<br /> <br /> Flyboy and myself were thinking of updating Dream Catchers to suit, and fixing some of the problems with the first draft. One of the things I felt was missing was an equipment section for non-Relic goodies. So here's the question to you forumites: What equipment should a faerie hunter carry?<br /> <br /> The obvious stuff would be iron weaponry - I'm also going to do bows since they seem to be popular and huntable elf-like fae will need them. But what else should the canny hunter know about? Horseshoes? <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Druids%27_egg\" target=\"_blank\">Druid's Eggs</a>?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Theme of Dream Catchers is You Don't Know the Rules, so I'm thinking that things that even other hunters will find unusual will be fitting but anything goes. Since there's no wordcount limit and the equipment rules have been revised since the Hunter core feel free to sneak a hunter essential or two into the list if you want it badly. Full write ups for your ideas are appreciated but not required <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T07:44:35-08:00","id":57431,"title":"","content":"I think that an hunter who hunt a Fey will have all kind of superstition equipment- horseshoes, 4 leaves clover, wear his cloths upside, things like that. You don't know the rules, so you gamble on what you do know and hope that there is a contract which makes sure you won't get hurt. I think that &quot;faerie hunters&quot; are going to relay upon superstition even more than other hunters, for they know that there is a chance that those believes may be grounded by a contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:05:51-08:00","id":57461,"title":"","content":"Since this is an equipment list the more specific examples (and possible mechanics) the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T17:42:07-08:00","id":57778,"title":"","content":"*cracks knuckles*<br /> <br /> The first thing that comes to mind is that, in order to deal with one's foe, one should take mind to look at past conflicts that one's foe has been in. For that reason, the first thing I suggest is a <b>Faerie Manual \u2014 </b>a term I will use to refer to a collection of notes, pictures and literature compiled into one book, all dealing with faeries. It can run from the gamut from resembling a witch's Book of Shadows, filled with ritual and mystical observation, to something more like a field manual \u2014 coldly based in fringe and non-fringe sciences. Depending on how extensive the collection is, it can provide a +1 to +3 bonus on all rolls dealing with investigating and tailing faeries. (+1 would be for a minor collection based mostly on folklore and first-hand accounts, while a +3 is akin to a Changeling having slipped you actual info to put in the manual.) The drawback would be that, if the wrong person found out you had a faerie manual, they might try to dispose of it \u2014 or you, if tehy felt threatened enough. Surely the Gentry would be interested in such knowledgeable and keen mortals, who might make for useful sentry or hard-working Wizened....<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're going to go stomping into fae territory, you're likely going to come across the Hedge. Though it may sound odd, <b>Enchanted</b> <b>Cold Iron Knives, Machetes and Hedge-Clippers </b>(I'm absolutely serious here) allows Hunters to (very temporarily) create a trod or clear out part of the Hedge. They carry a fraction of Arcadian power in their tools, the Wyrd recognizing them as &quot;shaping mechanisms&quot; and altering the Hedge as deemed fit. This kind of equipment is very, very difficult to come by, as you need a Changeling with a high-enough Wyrd score (I'm thinking 6+) to imbue mortals with the power to shape the Hedge. (Unless I'm missing something in actual Changeling lore.) Shaping the Hedge is a Strength+Occult action \u2014 Strength to cut through the supernaturally-thick vines, Occult so you know when and where to cut (and not have your path poof out from under you) \u2014 and for mortals, it should be an arduous, extended action. Dramatic failure is especially steep; due to the ever-shifting nature of the Hedge, if you screw up bad enough, you will lose a point of Humanity (if using pre-GM rules) or suffer a breaking point (GM rules). An alternative to the latter, for especially sadistic STs, is to have soul loss as a result of dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> And who is to say that all cold iron is equal? One of the most potent types of iron one can use is <b>Meteoric Iron</b>, poetically known as &quot;sky-iron&quot;. It is so potent, a dab of this in powdered form, applied to the end of any blade (iron or otherwise), will deal double Aggravated damage in a manner similar to how W:tF's Pure take damage from silver. Entire weapons constructed from sky-iron do devastating damage to Changelings, and even more so to Gentry. Sprinkled on a path through the Hedge, or painted onto the edges of a doorway into the Thorns, it can make the way through <i>permanent</i>, so long as the applicator of said sky-iron still lives. The first drawback of this is obvious \u2014 it's not always easy to come across meteorites with iron in them \u2014 and the second is a bit more occult in nature. The heat of entry into Earth's atmosphere actually slips away some of the material's &quot;cold&quot; properties, as it has been &quot;worked&quot; by coming into contact with the sphere of mortal influence. (This may have not been so in olden times, but ever since Man was able to launch some sort of material object high enough to the atmosphere [like a plane], Earth's own sky, by the Wyrd's working of things, is considered part of Man's domain. That means that Hedge portals could pop up in the clouds; be wary.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 01-25-2014, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T00:19:23-08:00","id":57956,"title":"","content":"Are you hunting changelings or faeries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T03:26:01-08:00","id":58005,"title":"","content":"Both of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T09:16:35-08:00","id":58772,"title":"","content":"Well once they get their frailties anything's possible. One changeling can't resist doing what a mother tells them, another will take damage in the light of a full moon, and some will die if exposed to water, but only for long periods, etc. The sky's the limit. You wouldn't really need mechanics for something like a locket from a lost love or the boots of a man who died standing in them.<br /> <br /> But until then, iron. It's not an instant-win or anything, it doesn't even do extra damage, but relatively pure iron will go through changeling Contract or magic defenses, including things like hedgespun armor. Hand-forged iron does aggravated damage to True Fae. There's some optional rules in the Rites of Spring book, and explanations (like you can ward an area from faeries by placing a horseshoe under the gate or something), but if you're running Hunter it really depends on how much you want to base things on Changeling and how much you want to freeform it.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and it's important to remember cold iron cannot be conjured, transmuted or shaped by magic. I mean, it can, but it loses its status as 'cold iron' and just becomes regular iron, for the purposes of dealing with fae stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2014, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T21:14:01-08:00","id":61980,"title":"","content":"I saw a KS for a book that may be inspiring for possible Compact or Conspiracy status called Storykiller. Here's the address:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/532638631/storykiller?ref=discovery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...?ref=discovery</a><br /> <br /> I'm just saying, the name Storykiller might be a cool name for Changling hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}